living in a fast-paced digital world  it's easy to become completely  disconnected from nature but no matter  where you are there are plenty of  natural wonders to find all you have to  do is stop for a moment and look I bet  you've got a seashell somewhere at home  in the bathroom or on a bookshelf or  venture into your garden or local park  follow the silvery trails and you should  easily find an animal living inside an  elegant spiral shells are enduring links  to another world that begins on our  doorsteps and stretches to remote  corners of the planet there the vacated  homes of an amazing group of animals the  mollusks including riffing from oysters  and snails to strange creatures like sea  butterflies and Argonauts there are  mollusks living in the deepest oceans to  the tops of mountains and just about  everywhere in between and they've been  around for a very long time their direct  ancestors were roaming the Seas more  than half a billion years ago so that  beautiful object in your hand connects  you not only to the natural world today  but deep into the past to a time long  before us humans and our busy lives came  along  you
 

